% Example Lab: books, chapters and manuals (fictional)
%
% These four entries exist for two reasons, both of them #69's.
%
% They are the four entry types sslabdata has no venue rule for -- an entry
% in a collection, an entry in a book, a book and a manual -- and they carry
% the fields nothing in the compiler reads: editor, publisher, address,
% series, chapter, pages, edition, isbn, month and organization. So the
% round-trip probe in examples/consumers/ has something to lose.
%
% They also carry the external-collaborator fixtures. Priya Patel is one
% person on three works, written `Patel, Priya` on two of them and
% `Patel, P.` on the third. Pradeep Patel is a different person, sharing her
% first initial and her family name. The fourth scenario -- two different
% people listed on one work under one written name -- is the pair of
% `Lee, Lin` authors on nolan2020stairs, in conference.bib.

